# (0.26) Music on the Desktop (DESK=1; tests/mousegen.py makes tests/music26.keys from this;
# the card's Programs menu gets "Music=/BIN/MUSIC.PRG"). Music's window: content at about
# (120, 71). Shots (s):
#   1   9.0  Programs > Music: the empty player (--rev 9 and older: the alert "Music needs Lau")
#   2  15.0  Files: /Music, HORIZON.MOD opened (typed, Enter): it reaches the running Music
#            (/SYSTEM/OPEN.REQ) and plays: title, format, position, time, the meters
#   3  16.5  a moment later: the meters and the position moved
#   4  21.5  LAU.MOD opened in Files: the playlist has two songs, LAU.MOD plays
#   5  23.5  the Pause button: paused (the meters fall)
#   6  26.5  Play, then a click at 40% of the position bar: a seek (order 2 of 3)
#   7  29.0  the Samples tab: the module's sample names
#   8  32.0  the Playlist tab again; HORIZON.MOD double clicked in the playlist: it plays
#   9  40.0  Programs > Edit in front, text typed from 35 s to 39.5 s: Music plays on behind it
#            (the run's stderr, build/music26.err, has every Lau write with its time:
#            emu816 --log-lau-us; Edit is in front from about 33.5 s to 40.5 s)
#  10  42.0  a click on Music's status line: in front again, the time went on (no gap)
